    "result_text": "Done. I agreed with the single finding and fixed it.\n\n**Change:** Rewrote the trailing sentence of the `riskFlag` javadoc in `OwnerMapper.java`. The old text (\"A `null` stored value on either flag is treated as `false`\u2026\") was boilerplate copied from `bulkSignupWarning`/`capacityWarning`/`possibleDuplicate`, each of which guards one stored `owner.getX()` boolean. `riskFlag` has no stored value and composes three derived signals, so that wording was inaccurate. It now reads:\n\n> The result composes those three sub-flags rather than reading a stored value, so it is always non-null (and thus always present in the response) for a non-null owner.\n\nNo behaviour changed \u2014 the suite is still green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`, `BUILD SUCCESS`).",
